<title>UK: EBRD 1997 GDP, INFLATION FORECASTS FOR E.EUROPE.</title>
<headline>EBRD 1997 GDP, INFLATION FORECASTS FOR E.EUROPE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are economic</p>
<p>forecasts for 1997 and 1996 for countries of eastern Europe in</p>
<p>the annual transition report of the European Bank for</p>
<p>Reconstruction and Development, in percent. The inflation</p>
<p>figure in based on the change in the average consumer price</p>
<p>level.</p>
<p>				   GDP			Inflation</p>
<p>				1997     1996	   1997     1996</p>
<p>East Europe &amp; Baltics</p>
<p>Albania			9.0	5.0	    10.0     13.0</p>
<p>Bulgaria		     2.0     -4.0	    74.0     95.0</p>
<p>Croatia			6.0	5.0	     6.0	3.5</p>
<p>Czech Rep.		   5.3	5.1	     8.2	9.0</p>
<p>Estonia			4.0	3.0	    21.0     26.0</p>
<p>Macedonia		    5.0	3.0	     3.0	4.0</p>
<p>Hungary			3.0	1.5	    17.0     24.0</p>
<p>Latvia			 3.0	1.0	    16.0     19.0</p>
<p>Lithuania		    4.0	1.5	    24.0     28.0</p>
<p>Poland			 5.0	5.0	    18.0     21.0</p>
<p>Romania			3.5	4.5	    35.0     40.0</p>
<p>Slovakia		     4.5	5.5	     6.5	7.0</p>
<p>Slovenia		     3.5	3.0	     7.0     10.0</p>
<p>Former Soviet Union</p>
<p>Armenia			7.0	6.5	    14.0     25.0</p>
<p>Azerbaijan		   4.0     -3.5	    12.0     20.0</p>
<p>Belarus			2.0     -5.0	    40.0     70.0</p>
<p>Georgia		     10.0	8.0	    15.0     50.0</p>
<p>Kazakstan		    1.0	0.5	    20.0     40.0</p>
<p>Kyrgyzstan		   8.0	2.0	    20.0     30.0</p>
<p>Moldova			4.0	4.0	    15.0     25.0</p>
<p>Russia			 3.0     -3.0	    22.0     45.0</p>
<p>Tajikistan		  -3.0     -7.0	   150.0    700.0</p>
<p>Turkmentistan		3.0	0.0	   250.0    500.0</p>
<p>Ukraine			1.0     -7.0	    50.0     90.0</p>
<p>Uzbekistan		   1.0     -1.0	    30.0     50.0</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Thatcher, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770 (fax</p>
